# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bawthub tenant manifest — single source of truth for ONE tenant.
#
#   cp tenant.env.example tenant.env   # then fill in, then ./bootstrap.sh
#
# Every value is a plain env var so it is (a) sourced by bootstrap for control
# flow and (b) interpolated by docker compose. No secrets live in git — required
# secrets are blank until you fill them; commented examples are not active.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── MODE (REQUIRED) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# prod = baked images, mount-free. dev = the same stack with llm-bawt source
# mounted into app and bridge; set DEV_SOURCE_DIR to the Docker host's checkout.
# Dev is for testing worktree code, not an image release.
MODE=prod
#DEV_SOURCE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/llm-bawt  # required with MODE=dev

# Compose project/container prefix; pick a unique name for a second tenant.
# Each tenant also needs different FRONTEND_PORT, SERVICE_PORT and MCP_PORT.
TENANT_NAME=bawthub

# Immutable core images (native amd64 + arm64, published from tested source).
# Images are built on demand for an exact commit; see README "Image pins (on-demand builds)".
# The app is the standard llm-bawt image, not a tenant-specific fork.
# app + agent-bridge + ops-worker source: bawthub/llm-bawt 15dd8b97a9b0d8742746f987ce2b189e86958b36
# (Tenant app image run 44837865343 attempt 1; all from the same commit so the bridge's
# run contract matches the app's).
# frontend source: bawthub/bawthub e4b0786e64fab18e4e7b092e6c032c6c03aefb94
# Canonical release image ghcr.io/bawthub/frontend:v0.1.124 (Release frontend
# image; amd64+arm64 index, the same stream production uses).
# Release run 44638571247 attempt 1.
# Existing tenants on the legacy ghcr.io/bawthub/tenant-frontend digest stay
# valid until they repin; that package is no longer published.
APP_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/app@sha256:33a700c96707d5668a472a00b5edbe06cd21cbbf42dbbd05f6499857d0b04c02
TENANT_FRONTEND_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/frontend@sha256:39ec16632897c955b5212e31da2d28f90cfc923297566dddc26bb852cfef0354
# REQUIRED: the agent bridge that runs the setup wizard's first bot (an agent).
# Published by llm-bawt's Tenant app image workflow (multiarch), pinned with the
# app above. Repin both together.
AGENT_BRIDGE_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/agent-bridge@sha256:c4940a023fbf17a5270b573843392eb7ed5222bcaa40939b4442197b598c86e1
# Test tenants only: build on this host with deploy/build-local.sh and paste
# its output here (localhost/bawthub/<component>:<sha> refs). See README
# "Local images". Never set this on a production tenant.
#IMAGE_SOURCE=local

# ── Voice (CPU-first) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pocket needs no GPU or operator-supplied cloning recording. The published
# CPU_STT_IMAGE_REF below enables local English microphone input. VOICE=off
# omits the voice backend, VOICE=external proxies an operator-provided backend.
VOICE=pocket
# Ops runner (approval-gated restarts with receipts). On by default; its
# ops-reconciler is the only container that mounts the Docker socket.
# TENANT_OPS=0 leaves it out (a rerun removes an existing runner), and service
# restarts then need a bootstrap rerun.
#TENANT_OPS=1
# REQUIRED unless TENANT_OPS=0: the per-job ops worker, published by the same
# llm-bawt Tenant app image run as the app. Repin all three together.
OPS_WORKER_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/ops-worker@sha256:e33737facb2ef358d0d80360e1d771487a413068a3d15f5a8eae4a981602ac03
# Agent tools: a headless browser (Playwright MCP) and a web crawler (Crawl4AI)
# for agent bots, CPU only. On by default; AGENT_TOOLS=0 leaves both out (a
# rerun removes them). Their Crawl4AI bearer is derived, never set here.
# Multiarch (amd64 + arm64) upstream digests.
#AGENT_TOOLS=1
PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_IMAGE_REF=docker.io/mcp/playwright@sha256:8771dc4666e7c11440bfc6a0c6b00480e9a15b8891b45f29a52d7d995f8d1492
CRAWL4AI_IMAGE_REF=docker.io/unclecode/crawl4ai:0.9.0@sha256:385042cba2a216c257ccb77b0135dec5228ee25bf675edbc7487eb155bd5e644
# Voice images (Pocket TTS, voice backend, Vosk CPU microphone input) published
# together by Tenant voice images run 44241914090 from BawtHub source
# 3fcbef341ad324ca0e732371e7c08cb33392bcba (v0.1.119). The voice backend
# authenticates its app probes, so it works with the sign-in default. These
# are verified native amd64 + arm64 index digests; no local-image or
# build-it-yourself tenant fallback is needed.
POCKET_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/pocket-tts@sha256:2a10c2487783885a519685e83954754266038b9bd8d2057123e912a9e4c2f9f8
# The voice backend alone is repinned to Tenant voice images run 44633664754
# from source ceb98ab9d2a80678fdecf163a91998525ba10909 (provider-aware TTS
# health, so a Pocket-only tenant reports healthy).
VOICE_BACKEND_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/voice-backend@sha256:7132b0b4e94c22df825bcb59feb567c362f4e21d8c574e312d7582d32e121fab
# Optional for existing manifests; enabled by default in this new-tenant example.
# Leaving it unset preserves text-in/voice-out for existing tenant manifests.
# CPU STT alone is repinned to Tenant voice images run 44633664754 from
# source ceb98ab9d2a80678fdecf163a91998525ba10909 (adds libatomic1 so Vosk
# loads on arm64; each architecture's build loads the model).
CPU_STT_IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/bawthub/cpu-stt@sha256:1d98ba0c882dabbd3bb9c76616cc1d02736af9ec8b36589461e5f6fba1e43ac6
#EXTERNAL_VOICE_URL=https://<your-voice-backend>  # only for VOICE=external

# ── Bridge SSH identity (dev mode only) ────────────────────────────────────
# Agent bridges need an SSH key to reach their own host (deploys/ops) and other
# LAN hosts. Because bootstrap runs ON the host, `up` generates a DEDICATED
# ed25519 keypair and authorizes it for a dedicated agent user (AGENT_USER),
# created without Docker access. Needs sudo once. The dev overlay mounts the key dir read-only into each bridge.
# The printed public key is for OTHER targets (other LAN hosts, GitHub deploy keys).
#BRIDGE_SSH=1                                   # set 0 to skip provisioning
#BRIDGE_SSH_KEY_DIR=<abs-path>                  # default: deploy/.bridge-ssh (gitignored)
#AGENT_USER=bawthub-agent                       # host account the bridges SSH in as
# Opt-in: let agents run docker on this host via sudo. Docker access is root on
# the host. Revoke: sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/50-docker-via-sudo
#AGENT_HOST_DOCKER=0

# ── Published ports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SERVICE_PORT=8642
MCP_PORT=8001
FRONTEND_PORT=3000
# Agent-facing URLs derive from FRONTEND_HOST and FRONTEND_PORT by default.
# Set a reachable LAN/FQDN host when external agents cannot use localhost.
#FRONTEND_HOST=localhost
#AGENT_ORIGIN=http://your-host.example:3000
# Shared media links use AGENT_ORIGIN. Behind a TLS proxy, port forward or NAT,
# set the address people open instead; sign-in accepts only this origin.
#LLM_BAWT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://bawthub.your-domain.example

# ── Houses (agent containers) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Capped containers a claude-code bot can move into with its self_house tool;
# an emptied house restarts itself. Each house serves a task worktree's
# frontend preview (house-preview) on its own port of AGENT_ORIGIN's host:
# h1 on HOUSE_PREVIEW_PORT_BASE, h2 on the next port, and so on. Previews use
# sign-in sessions on that origin. HOUSES=0 runs none.
#HOUSES=2
# Per-house memory cap, a ceiling rather than a reservation. Default: half
# this host's memory, 2–4 GiB. A bot running a BawtHub preview needs about 3g.
#HOUSE_MEMORY=3g
# Each house starts its occupant's preview by itself. auto (default) leaves
# that off on hosts under 6 GiB, where a preview would run the tenant out of
# memory; on or off forces it.
#HOUSE_PREVIEW=auto
#HOUSE_PREVIEW_PORT_BASE=3101
# Behind a TLS proxy, name each preview instead ({id} = h1.., {port} = its
# published port, which the proxy forwards to):
#HOUSE_PREVIEW_ORIGIN_TEMPLATE=https://{id}.preview.example.com

# ── Access ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# signin (default for a new install): everyone signs in. The first `up` prints
# a one-time setup code for creating the owner account; the app API and MCP
# ports listen on this host's loopback only.
# trusted-lan: the earlier sessionless mode with a user picker and the app
# ports on every interface. Trusted networks only; never expose it publicly.
# An existing tenant must choose one explicitly; bootstrap remembers it.
#ACCESS=signin
# Publish the app API and MCP ports on every interface under signin too.
#PUBLISH_APP_PORTS=1
# Under signin, house preview ports sit behind a sign-in gate; off leaves them open.
#BAWT_HOUSE_PREVIEW_GATE=off

# ── Local database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LOCAL postgres container holds both databases. The frontend gets a
# SEPARATE database inside it; bootstrap creates it, verifies isolation, and
# applies committed migrations. Never set FRONTEND_POSTGRES_DATABASE to the app
# database name. Ignored when EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_* is filled in.
# The password is generated on a new install and kept 0600 as .postgres-password
# in the tenant secrets directory. Set it here only for an existing database
# whose password is not stored there; a stored file must match.
LLM_BAWT_POSTGRES_USER=llm_bawt
#LLM_BAWT_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<only-for-an-existing-database>
LLM_BAWT_POSTGRES_DATABASE=llm_bawt
FRONTEND_POSTGRES_DATABASE=bawthub_frontend

# ── Tenant secrets directory ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated secrets live 0600 in deploy/ for the default tenant (gitignored),
# or under ~/.config/bawthub/<TENANT_NAME>/ for other names. The directory is
# the one holding BAWTHUB_MASTER_KEY_FILE (its historical name); override it
# only to move a tenant's secrets.
#BAWTHUB_MASTER_KEY_FILE=<abs-path>/.master-key
# Legacy only: the retired pgcrypto vault's key. Bootstrap no longer generates
# it. Set it only to import an old tenant's vault whose .master-key file is
# missing; `./bootstrap.sh import-vault` stores it 0600 and imports.
#BAWTHUB_MASTER_KEY=<legacy-vault-key-only-for-import-vault>

# ── Agent runtime secrets (generated in the secrets directory; back them up) ──
# LLM_BAWT_SECRET_KEY encrypts stored provider credentials (OAuth logins, API
# keys added in the UI). On first `up` bootstrap adopts the key an earlier app
# start left in its config volume, or generates one, and writes it 0600 to
# .llm-bawt-secret-key. Losing it makes every stored credential unreadable.
# BRIDGE_CLAUDE_TOKEN_SECRET is the app↔agent-bridge broker secret
# (.bridge-token-secret). Set either only when restoring a tenant; a value
# that disagrees with the stored file or volume refuses to start.
#LLM_BAWT_SECRET_KEY=<pin-only-when-restoring>
#BRIDGE_CLAUDE_TOKEN_SECRET=<pin-only-when-restoring>
#LLM_BAWT_SECRET_KEY_FILE=<abs-path>
#BRIDGE_CLAUDE_TOKEN_SECRET_FILE=<abs-path>

# ── Provider keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Connect providers in the app (Settings → Providers); it stores them encrypted
# under LLM_BAWT_SECRET_KEY. Keys written here still work, but `up` warns about
# any secret value it finds in this file (names only, never values).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXTERNAL service opt-in
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL-FIRST: leave a block blank → that service runs as a local container.
# Fill a block → the local container is dropped and the service is repointed
# at the existing external one (for example, a database you already run).

# ── Postgres (app memory + pgvector store) ─────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment + fill to drop the local pgvector container and use an external DB.
# Use an IP or a fully qualified name: tenant containers get no DNS search
# domain (TASK-1561), so a short host name won't resolve.
#EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_HOST=<host-ip>
#EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_PORT=5432
#EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_USER=<user>
#EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<PLACEHOLDER>
#EXTERNAL_POSTGRES_DATABASE=<db>

# ── Frontend Prisma DB (must be a DIFFERENT DB than the app's) ─────────────
# Pre-create this dedicated database with vector extension privileges for the
# frontend user. Bootstrap refuses shared and previously unmanaged layouts;
# it never copies old tables (existing installs: TASK-1127).
# Full DATABASE_URL; URL-encode special chars in the password (# → %23).
#EXTERNAL_FRONTEND_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<PLACEHOLDER>@<host-ip>:5432/<db>?schema=public

# ── Embeddings (CPU sidecar — vector memory search on CPU-only hosts) ───────
# On by default: the published CPU embed image (MiniLM, 384-dim, model baked
# in, linux amd64 + arm64), digest-pinned. Comment it out to run without it;
# the stack still boots and memory degrades to non-vector search. With
# IMAGE_SOURCE=local, localhost/bawthub/embed:<tag> works too.
EMBED_IMAGE=ghcr.io/bawthub/embed@sha256:6c8892d20b53176c41421cd22c0dcc69504c228769d75c7e380be022523f2e64

# ── GPU ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CPU tenant installer rejects GPU=1; the optional voice stack is separate.
#GPU=1

# ── Redis ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#EXTERNAL_REDIS_URL=redis://<host-ip>:6379/0

# ── Future EXTERNAL_* blocks (design placeholders — not wired yet) ──────────
# Embeddings:  EXTERNAL_EMBEDDINGS_URL=...
# Storage/S3:  STORAGE_BACKEND=s3 / EXTERNAL_S3_*=...   (default STORAGE_BACKEND=fs)
# Search:      EXTERNAL_SEARCH_URL=...
# Home Assist: EXTERNAL_HA_URL=... / EXTERNAL_HA_TOKEN=...
# Voice:       VOICE=external + EXTERNAL_VOICE_URL (configured above)
